 der: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 30px 0;"/><h3 style="f
 ont-size: 16px; color: #004d98;">Live Interactive Capabilities Showca
 se (Studio Engine)</h3><p style="color: #4a5568; margin-bottom: 16px;
  font-size: 12px;">Explore the active visual representations of Anaha
 ta ASI Studio operating directly inside Apache NetBeans:</p><div styl
 e="margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px 
 solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bott
 om: 6px; font-size: 13px;">[1] Singularity Engine: Dynamic JIT Java C
 ompiler</h4><p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10
 px 0;">The model compiles and executes raw Java code directly inside 
 your running NetBeans JVM utilizing our custom child-first ClassLoade
 r. Build, test, and hot-load live tools, Java swing panels, or comple
 x dependency algorithms on-the-fly.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.u
 no/screenshots/netbeans/NbJava.png" target="_blank"><img src="https:/
 /asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/NbJava.png" alt="[1] Sin
 gularity Engine: Dynamic JIT Java Compiler" width="650" border="0" />
 </a></div><div style="margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background:
  #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-
 top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 13px;">[2] Multimodal Vision: 
 Real-Time Screen & Region Sharing</h4><p style="font-size: 11px; colo
 r: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Share physical screens, specific mon
 itors, or custom rectangular regions with the ASI. Perfect for provid
 ing real-time visual feedback on Swing UI renders, layouts, or compil
 er states.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/N
 etBeansLiveScreenSharingAdrianaLima.png" target="_blank"><img src="ht
 tps://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/NetBeansLiveScreenS
 haringAdrianaLima.png" alt="[2] Multimodal Vision: Real-Time Screen &
  Region Sharing" width="650" border="0" /></a></div><div style="margi
 n-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e
 2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-size: 13px;">[3] Atomic Context: Visual Resource Highlighting</
 h4><p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Co
 mplete visual context awareness. Files loaded into the active AI cont
 ext automatically light up with a vibrant indicator directly inside t
 he NetBeans Projects, Files, and Favorites views.</p><a href="https:/
 /asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/InContextResourcesVisualization
 .png" target="_blank"><img src="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/n
 etbeans/thumbs/InContextResourcesVisualization.png" alt="[3] Atomic C
 ontext: Visual Resource Highlighting" width="650" border="0" /></a></
 div><div style="margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0
 ; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 13px;">[4] Real-Time 3D & Hardware P
 rototyping (LWJGL)</h4><p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; mar
 gin: 0 0 10px 0;">With built-in LWJGL, GLFW, and OpenGL dependencies,
  the agent can write, compile, and run raw, real-time 3D rendering wi
 ndows and game prototypes directly on the host JVM.</p><a href="https
 ://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/NetBeansBundledLWJGL.png" tar
 get="_blank"><img src="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/t
 humbs/NetBeansBundledLWJGL.png" alt="[4] Real-Time 3D & Hardware Prot
 otyping (LWJGL)" width="650" border="0" /></a></div><div style="margi
 n-bottom: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e
 2e8f0;"><h4 style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-size: 13px;">[5] Agentic Feedback: Inline AI Code Annotations</
 h4><p style="font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Mo
 del suggestions, code explanations, and diagnostics are painted dynam
 ically directly onto your source code lines within the NetBeans edito
 r, acting as non-intrusive guide markers.</p><a href="https://asi.ana
 hata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/InlineAIAnnotations.png" target="_blank
 "><img src="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumbs/Inlin
 eAIAnnotations.png" alt="[5] Agentic Feedback: Inline AI Code Annotat
 ions" width="650" border="0" /></a></div><div style="margin-bottom: 2
 0px; padding: 12px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><h4
  style="color: #004d98; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size:
  13px;">[6] Self-Healing Filesystem tracking (NbHandle)</h4><p style=
 "font-size: 11px; color: #4a5568; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Every resource
  handle in context is bound to a native NetBeans FileObject. If you d
 rag-and-drop, rename, cut, or paste a file across projects, the handl
 e auto-heals and preserves context.</p><a href="https://asi.anahata.u
 no/screenshots/netbeans/NbHandleForFileObjectIntegration.png" target=
 "_blank"><img src="https://asi.anahata.uno/screenshots/netbeans/thumb
 s/NbHandleForFileObjectIntegration.png" alt="[6] Self-Healing Filesys
 tem tracking (NbHandle)" width="650" border="0" /></a></div><div styl
